  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards 2030: Transformative actions and partnerships to deliver the SDGs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A two-day event at Wilton Park in March 2024 designed to maintain momentum from the SDG Summit on generating lessons learnt, best practice and evidence to determine what works for achieving the SDGs.  We will convene a wide range of relevant actors and use the event to build partnerships across governments, civil society, the private sector and academia, including those from the middle ground&#x2019; as a &#x2018;coalition of the willing&#x2019; to accelerate SDG progress. Building on themes  from the FCDO Directors&#x2019; internal SDG discussion paper (September 2023) and the 2023 White Paper, the intention is for these discussions to begin to flesh out specific policy recommendations that can be discussed more widely in relevant global fora throughout 2024 (G20, LLDC3, SIDS4, Summit of the Future) to inform a more pro-active and evidence based response to the call to turbocharge SDG delivery.</narrative>
  </description>
